# 📋 Architecture Plan: DynamoDB to S3 Tables Drain Pipeline

## 1. Architectural Overview
This pipeline architecture uses an event-driven ingestion pattern. Data is captured immediately upon being written to DynamoDB and is streamed continuously into S3 Tables.

[ Application ] 
       │ (High-velocity writes)
       ▼
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│  Amazon DynamoDB             │ ───► Free Auto-Cleanup (TTL)
└──────────────────────────────┘
       │ (Change Data Capture)
       ▼
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│  DynamoDB Streams            │
└──────────────────────────────┘
       │ (Real-time events)
       ▼
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│  Amazon Data Firehose        │ ───► Optional: AWS Lambda Data Transformation
└──────────────────────────────┘
       │ (Micro-batching & Parquet formatting)
       ▼
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│  Amazon S3 Tables (Iceberg)  │ ───► Automatic File Compaction
└──────────────────────────────┘


## 2. Component Design & Configuration

### A. Amazon DynamoDB (The Write Buffer)
DynamoDB acts strictly as a transient landing zone optimized for fast ingestion.
*   **Capacity Mode:** Set to **On-Demand** if traffic is highly spiky, or **Provisioned** with Auto-Scaling if workloads are predictable.
*   **DynamoDB Streams:** **Enabled**. Set the View Type to `New Image` or `New and Old Images`. This tracks changes without consuming table Read Capacity Units (RCUs).
*   **Time to Live (TTL):** **Enabled**. Include an `ttl_timestamp` attribute on every item (calculated as `epoch_now + 86400` for a 24-hour buffer). DynamoDB will purge expired records **for free** without impacting production performance.

### B. Amazon Data Firehose (The Delivery Stream)
Firehose natively bridges the streaming data into structured cloud storage.
*   **Source:** Configured to ingest natively from the **DynamoDB Stream**.
*   **Destination:** **Amazon S3 Tables**.
*   **Buffer Hints:** Configure the delivery stream to flush data to S3 based on whichever threshold is met first:
    *   *Size:* **128 MB** (creates healthy file footprints)
    *   *Interval:* **900 seconds (15 minutes)** (or lower depending on your latency requirements)
*   **Data Format Conversion:** Enabled. Firehose can automatically convert the incoming JSON stream into **Apache Parquet** format on-the-fly, reducing downstream S3 storage costs and accelerating analytics performance.

### C. Amazon S3 Tables (The Analytics Lake)
S3 Tables provide a managed home for your transactional and analytical data using open table formats.
*   **Table Format:** **Apache Iceberg** (native to S3 Tables).
*   **Maintenance Policies:** **Automatic Compaction Enabled**. Because streaming data creates small physical files, S3 Tables automatically merge smaller parts into large Parquet blocks background-style, preventing query degradation.

